{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaPUecyKGSpdHPGh9BFz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `double_eq` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem double_eq (n : Nat) : double n = 2 * n := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => rfl\n  | succ n ih => simp only [double, ih]; omega\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on `n`:\n- **Base case:** `double 0` is `0` by definition, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **Inductive step:** the definition of `double` turns `double (n + 1)` into `double n + 2`. Using the inductive hypothesis, that becomes `2 * n + 2`, and `omega` shows it equals `2 * (n + 1)`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":7840,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"output_tokens":240,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"317f37aa-24b3-45cd-b350-3c01f326db8a","uuid":"43339bc0-44ee-4668-8dd0-6f7d1394d0d0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:24:16.903Z","request_id":"req_011CgaPUeP5Qsf2PT1ajmNHd"}
